    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d678">

                <pb facs="0963" n="827" xml:id="pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/320: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Paraguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kreeck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Asunción</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-30T19:00:00-03:50">December 30, 1928—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 31—2:34 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>45. Your telegram No. 21<anchor n="8" xml:id="d678-f1"/> received December 30, 6
                    p.m. Paraguayan Minister for Foreign Affairs telegraphed its representative
                    December 29, 3 p.m. to sign protocol. Delay arises from consideration of the
                    meager provisions for the investigation they being limited to incidents other
                    than the real cause of conflict thus permitting aggressions and molestations to
                    continue as formerly thereby causing no real benefit to Paraguay by such
                    investigation.</p>
                <p>I am convinced this view is well established and that permanent peace will not be
                    found until the cause has been removed which can only be done by the
                    Conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kreeck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
